{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfggF3znfSky4Xz9EYqgr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive extension that mirrors the existing `bulkSignupWarning` sibling flag end-to-end, which is exactly what a maintainer of this codebase would expect:\n\n- **Owner model**: field, getter/setter, and `toString` entry are all placed directly alongside `bulkSignupWarning`, following the same `Boolean` column convention.\n- **OwnerMapper**: `formatCapacityWarning` sits next to `formatBulkSignupWarning` and is structurally identical (null-coalescing to `false`), with matching `@Mapping` forward expression and reverse-direction `ignore`. The logic lives in the right unit — resolution/formatting stays in the mapper.\n- **Controller**: the `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD` constant is co-located with `CITY_CAPACITY` and documented in the same style. Good touch extracting `ownersInCity` into a local so `countOwnersInCity` is called once rather than duplicated, and the warning assignment is correctly sequenced after the hard-reject return (so the flag only reflects the 40–49 band). Keeping it in the controller is consistent with where `bulkSignupWarning` and the capacity check already live.\n- **Schema + OpenAPI**: the column is added uniformly across all four dialects and the API schema entry matches the `readOnly` boolean convention of its neighbors.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all accumulation beyond the already-established warning-flag pattern, and nothing is misplaced. Structure is already clean."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9855,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9855},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null